---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, absoluteUrl } from '../lib/site';

const ld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Editorial Policy',
  url: absoluteUrl('/editorial-policy'),
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: SITE.name, url: absoluteUrl('/') },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.name, url: absoluteUrl('/') },
};
---

<Base
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How MyCryptoSignal produces its content: original market briefs from our own data, attributed news digests, our AI-assistance disclosure, authorship, corrections, and ownership."
  path="/editorial-policy"
  jsonLd={[ld]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Standards &amp; transparency</p>
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 12 October 2026</p>

      <p>
        MyCryptoSignal is a crypto market-data publication operated by {SITE.operator}. This page explains
        what we publish, how we produce it, who is responsible, and how we handle corrections. It applies to
        every article, market brief, digest, and signal on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>What we publish</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Market briefs (original).</strong> Short daily reports written <em>only</em> from numbers we
          collect ourselves — prices, moves, and market breadth. Our own prose about our own data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>News digests (attributed).</strong> A brief summary of a story published elsewhere, in our own
          words, always naming and linking the original source. We summarise and link; we do not reproduce or
          rewrite other publishers' articles.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Signals (informational).</strong> A deterministic daily direction word per tracked coin
          (Rising, Falling, Steady, or Choppy) with the measured reason. Signals describe what the numbers show.
          They are not predictions and not advice.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How content is produced</h2>
      <p>
        Content is produced by an automated, supervised publishing pipeline. We collect market data from
        public price APIs, compute standard indicators deterministically, and use AI language models to write
        plain-language summaries of those numbers. Every figure in a brief or signal originates from our
        collected data at the timestamp shown. Dates and times are genuine and never backdated or artificially
        refreshed.
      </p>

      <h2>AI assistance disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        We use AI to draft text from structured data. The pipeline is constrained by fixed policy rules
        (no advice, no predictions, no hype, no invented numbers, mandatory source attribution) and the output
        is reviewed and operated by a human editor, who is accountable for what is published. We do not use AI
        to fabricate quotes, sources, or events.
      </p>

      <h2>Authorship and accountability</h2>
      <p>
        Market briefs are published under the <strong>MyCryptoSignal Data Desk</strong>. Digests are published
        under the <strong>MyCryptoSignal Editorial</strong> desk. {SITE.operator} is the publisher and is
        accountable for all content. Editorial questions and corrections: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Sources and attribution</h2>
      <p>
        Every digest names its source and links directly to the original article. Price and market figures come
        from our own collection from public exchange and market-data APIs. Where a non-price fact is included,
        it is attributed to the named source.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If we publish something inaccurate, we correct it and note the change. To request a correction, email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a> with the article URL and the issue. We
        aim to respond promptly.
      </p>

      <h2>Commercial &amp; funding</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.operator} owns and operates MyCryptoSignal. Our revenue comes from affiliate commissions on
        the <a href="/tools-and-partners">Tools &amp; Partners</a> page, from sponsorships named on that same
        page, and from paid tiers of our data API. Our signals, direction calls and briefs receive no
        commercial input and are never for sale.
      </p>
      <p>
        The firewall rule, in one sentence: <strong>every commercial or affiliate link lives only on the
        Tools &amp; Partners page — never on a signal, brief, news or market page, and never beside a
        direction word.</strong> Compensated links are labelled at the point of contact and carry
        <code>rel="sponsored nofollow"</code>. See <a href="/disclosure">How we make money</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Independence and funding</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.operator} funds and operates MyCryptoSignal. We do not accept payment to publish, suppress, or
        alter editorial content, and we do not publish sponsored articles. Commercial products (such as the
        data API) are disclosed and kept separate from editorial content.
      </p>

      <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is financial, investment, legal, or tax advice, and nothing is an offer or
        solicitation to buy or sell any asset. Crypto markets are volatile and carry significant risk. Do your
        own research. See our <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a> and <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
